              "content-type": "text/html; charset=utf-8"
            },
            "body": "<!doctype html><html><head><title>A tiny Lisp in 200 lines of C</title><meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lispy.example/img/lisp.png\"></head><body><article><h1>A tiny Lisp in 200 lines of C</h1><p>This post walks through a minimal Lisp interpreter: a reader, eval, apply and a garbage collector in about 200 lines of portable C.</p><img src=\"https://lispy.example/img/lisp.png\" alt=\"cover\"></article></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "https://ops-weekly.example/2026/11/agents-replace-cron",
            "status": 200,
            "headers": {
              "content-type": "text/html; charset=utf-8"
            },
            "body": "<!doctype html><html><head><title>We replaced 140 cron jobs with AI agents</title><meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://ops-weekly.example/img/agents-cron-cover.png\"></head><body><article><h1>We replaced 140 cron jobs with AI agents</h1><p>Over six months our ops team moved 140 brittle cron scripts to a workflow engine where LLM agents triage failures, open tickets and retry with backoff. Incidents fell 38% and on-call pages halved.</p><p>The hard parts were idempotency, secrets handling and keeping a human approval step for anything that deletes data.</p><img src=\"https://ops-weekly.example/img/agents-cron-cover.png\" alt=\"cover\"></article></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "https://birdwatch.example/autumn-migration",
            "status": 200,
            "headers": {
              "content-type": "text/html; charset=utf-8"
            },
            "body": "<!doctype html><html><head><title>Tracking the autumn bird migration</title><meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://birdwatch.example/img/pi.png\"></head><body><article><h1>Tracking the autumn bird migration</h1><p>A Raspberry Pi, a microphone and an open-source classifier logged 9,400 night flight calls in October.</p><img src=\"https://birdwatch.example/img/pi.png\" alt=\"cover\"></article></body></html>"
          }
